---
description: Hyper Light Card is a custom Lovelace card for Home Assistant to control SignalRGB with dynamic color theming
globs: /**/*
alwaysApply: false
---
Project Structure & Architecture:

Core Components:

- @src/hyper-light-card.ts: Main component class
- @src/state.ts: State management model
- @src/state-manager.ts: Manages state changes and HA interactions
- @src/color-manager.ts: Handles color extraction from effects
- @src/utils.ts: Utility functions and helpers
- @src/config.ts: Configuration interface
- @src/hyper-light-card-editor.ts: Card configuration UI

Build System:

- @vite.config.ts: Build configuration
- @package.json: Dependencies and scripts

Architecture Constraints:

1. Follow Lit component patterns
2. Maintain reactivity via @state/@property
3. Keep state logic separate from UI
4. Use ColorThief for palette extraction
5. Ensure accessibility in color contrast

The card dynamically adapts its UI based on extracted colors from SignalRGB effects, creating a cohesive visual experience.
